# overlay-exclude.txt
#
# Copy this file to ~/.claude/config/overlay-exclude.txt and add one substring
# per line. cast-overlay-sync.sh skips any file whose relative path (from
# ~/.claude/) contains a listed substring. This keeps work-project memory dirs
# out of your personal cloud backup.
#
# Format:
#   - One substring per line
#   - Lines beginning with # are comments (skipped)
#   - Blank lines are skipped
#   - Substrings are matched with shell glob (*substring*)
#     against the relative path (e.g. projects/my-project/memory/foo.md)
#
# You can also set CAST_OVERLAY_EXCLUDE="substring1 substring2" in your
# environment; both sources are combined (union).
#
# Examples (all commented out — add your own below):
# work-project-dir-name
# another-work-project
